<urn:uxf:requirement:accessible-feedback-and-recovery:positive:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Rendered feedback exposes an understandable named outcome and its state, keeps focus at the actor's working context unless the actor requests movement, remains keyboard-operable, announces outcome and recovery information, and supplies an actionable recovery path for each error." <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:accessible-feedback-and-recovery:positive:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:accessible-feedback-and-recovery:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibleEvidenceClass> "implementation-conformance" <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:accessible-feedback-and-recovery:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Rendered feedback never makes colour the sole error signal, never leaves a terminal failure without reason and recovery, and never silently changes control or disclosure state." <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:accessible-feedback-and-recovery:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
