<urn:uxf:requirement:observational-operator-interpretation:positive:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibleEvidenceClass> "implementation-conformance" <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:observational-operator-interpretation:positive:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Rendered read-only observational output lets an operator access and interpret captured state, milestones and evidence through the product surface without entering or pasting commands. The same read-only surface exposes capture timestamp, source and scope; charts and tables preserve actual observed values and explicit missing or unknown values through accessible mobile drill-down, with keyboard, focus and assistive access to the same information." <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:observational-command-paste-prerequisite:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:observational-command-paste-prerequisite:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibleEvidenceClass> "implementation-conformance" <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
<urn:uxf:requirement:observational-command-paste-prerequisite:negative:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Rendered read-only observational output never requires command entry or command pasting to access or interpret captured state, milestones or evidence. Captured state must never appear as live state or live control; absent data must never appear as observed values, zero, success or hidden aggregate completeness. The presentation must not expose a live-control bridge, imply actuation, or use visual encoding alone to conceal missingness." <urn:uxf:graph:accessibility-i18n-risk> .
